      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, I don\u0027t get why? Is it related to this change?\n\nIIUC, we wanted to be explicit about updatable/min_sdk_version. When an apex is updatable, then it should set min_sdk_version even if it is \"current\". (However, \"current\" is discouraged because updatable apexes typically live longer beyond the finalized branches. And they need to set min_sdk_version to the first dessert they\u0027ve launched. So, \"current\" should be fixed to a concrete number(or codename) in other branches (e.g. aosp master).)",
      "parentUuid": "b0571a56_8f037a12",
